tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# The agent surface is derived from public/wiki on every build (see
# scripts/build-agent-api.mjs). Committing it would rewrite a 3 MB text file
# on every sync for no gain — the deploy regenerates it.
public/llms.txt
public/llms-full.txt
public/agent/

# The gate's verifier used to be ignored here, on the reasoning that a blob
# built from somebody's throwaway test passphrase is worse than none at all.
# True — and the cost was that no verifier ever reached the deploy, so the
# gate served ENTER ANYWAY to everybody and the lock on the front of the site
# was not a lock. This deployment now commits a real one deliberately, which
# is what the README always said to do.
#
# It is a ciphertext: committing it leaks nothing but the cost of guessing.
# To rotate, re-run `npm run gate:verify` with the new phrase in the
# environment and commit the result.

# THE GALLERY capture rig caches the CDN assets the old pages pull
.gallery-vendor/
